Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.10,0:00:05.38,ShortsHighlight,,0,0,0,,IN 1904, AN OLYMPIC RUNNER WON\NGOLD USING RAT POISON AND BRANDY.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.50,0:00:13.26,ShortsHighlight,,0,0,0,,THE ST. LOUIS MARATHON WAS A NINETY-DEGREE NIGHTMARE\NWITH ONLY ONE WATER STATION ACROSS TWENTY-SIX DUST-CHOKED MILES.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.37,0:00:17.61,ShortsHighlight,,0,0,0,,ONLY FOURTEEN OF\NTHIRTY-TWO COMPETITORS FINISHED ALIVE.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.56,0:00:23.37,ShortsHighlight,,0,0,0,,ONE RUNNER WAS CHASED A MILE OFF\NCOURSE INTO A CORNFIELD BY AGGRESSIVE STRAY DOGS.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.37,0:00:31.48,ShortsHighlight,,0,0,0,,MEANWHILE, A CUBAN POSTMAN RAN IN STREET BOOTS, STOPPED\NTO EAT APPLES, TOOK AN HOUR NAP, AND FINISHED FOURTH!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.48,0:00:39.00,ShortsHighlight,,0,0,0,,WHEN LEADER THOMAS HICKS BEGAN COLLAPSING, HIS HANDLERS\NADMINISTERED DOSES OF STRYCHNINE RAT POISON MIXED WITH BRANDY.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.17,0:00:45.42,ShortsHighlight,,0,0,0,,HALLUCINATING WILDLY AND BARELY CONSCIOUS, HICKS WAS CARRIED\NACROSS THE FINISH LINE TO CLAIM OLYMPIC GOLD.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.53,0:00:49.34,ShortsHighlight,,0,0,0,,IT REMAINS THE MOST\NCHAOTIC RACE IN ATHLETIC HISTORY.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.29,0:00:53.42,ShortsHighlight,,0,0,0,,FOLLOW CRAZZYDOCS FOR\NMORE WILD HISTORICAL BREAKTHROUGHS!